# Byte-exactness is the whole premise of this repo: prefix-safe merge compares
# session files byte for byte, and the CLIs always terminate lines with LF
# (findings/2026-08-06-spike-conclusions.md, OQ-8). A Windows checkout that
# silently rewrote line endings would turn every fixture into a false conflict.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures and sample session data are opaque bytes — never transform them.
tests/fixtures/** -text
*.jsonl -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they fail with `bad interpreter: ...^M`.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
